+## 3. Simplification Proposals and Focus Areas
+
+### 3.1 Active Directory vs OpenLDAP 1-Click Presets (Already Implemented)
+- **Status:** **Already Implemented** in `AuthCardEditorDrawer.tsx` (lines 746-755).
+- **Implementation Parity:** The 1-Click Presets bar already includes dedicated buttons for **Active Directory** (`data-testid="preset-active-directory"`) and **OpenLDAP** (`data-testid="preset-openldap"`). When selected, `applyPreset()` automatically populates:
+  - Standard schemes and ports: `ldaps://ad.corp.local:636` (Active Directory) and `ldaps://ldap.corp.local:636` (OpenLDAP), `transport_mode="ldaps"`.
+  - Canonical filters:
+    - Active Directory: `(&(objectCategory=person)(objectClass=user)(sAMAccountName={username}))`
+    - OpenLDAP: `(&(objectClass=person)(uid={username}))`
+  - Canonical attribute mappings:
+    - Active Directory: `subject_attribute="objectGUID"`, `email_attribute="mail"`, `display_name_attribute="displayName"`
+    - OpenLDAP: `subject_attribute="entryUUID"`, `email_attribute="mail"`, `display_name_attribute="cn"`
+- **Phase 2 Boundary:** No new presets required; retain existing implementations.
+
+### 3.2 `sort_rank` and Fractional Indexing
+- **Current UX Friction:** While the backend uses fractional indexing strings (e.g. `after: "0|i00001:"`) to order cards in `POST /api/v1/admin/auth-cards/{card_ref}/reorder`, raw rank values or confusing reordering mechanics should never burden the administrator.
+- **Simplification Strategy:** Expose clean drag-and-drop grab handles paired with accessible Up/Down keyboard buttons in `AuthStudioPage.tsx`. Completely encapsulate fractional indexing in the frontend service; administrators simply drag cards or click Up/Down to establish visual precedence.
+
+### 3.3 SPKI SHA-256 Pin vs CA Certificate PEM
+- **Status:** Collapsible disclosure `<AdvancedSection testId="auth-advanced-section">` is **Already Implemented** in `AuthCardEditorDrawer.tsx` (lines 1105, 1618-1662).
+- **Implementation Parity:** Both `card-spki-pin` (validated against 64-char hex digest `SPKI_REGEX = /^[A-Fa-f0-9]{64}$/`) and `card-ca-pem` reside cleanly inside `<AdvancedSection testId="auth-advanced-section">`.
+- **Phase 2 Scope:** Add client-side PEM header validation alerting users if a provided CA certificate block lacks `-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----` headers.
+
+### 3.4 Copyable OIDC Redirect URI (Callback URL)
+- **Status:** Dynamic URI computation and 1-click copy button (`data-testid="copy-callback-url-btn"`) are **Already Implemented** in `AuthCardEditorDrawer.tsx` (line 918).
+- **Implementation Parity:** The read-only input dynamically displays `${window.location.origin}/api/v1/auth/oidc/${slug}/callback` and updates reactively as the slug input changes.
+- **Phase 2 Scope:** Add an origin warning callout if running on `http://localhost` or a non-standard port, reminding administrators that IdPs require HTTPS or exact port registration.
+
+### 3.5 Anti-Lockout Safeguards and Break-Glass Warnings
+- **Current UX Friction:** Disabling or deleting an authentication card can trigger a `409 Conflict` (`LOCKOUT_PREVENTED`) from the backend if the action would leave the system without any functional administrative login method.
+- **Simplification Strategy:**
+  - Before an administrator disables or deletes a card, calculate client-side whether this card represents the last active administrative authentication card.
+  - If it is the last card, display an explicit **Break-Glass Warning** dialog explaining that at least one local administrator account or alternative active authentication card must remain configured to prevent lockout.
+  - Clarify the 3-layer anti-lockout architecture in inline help text: (1) Local Admin Card Invariant, (2) Active Administrator Principal Invariant, and (3) Active Session Step-Up.
+
+### 3.6 Password-Manager and Autofill Suppression
+- **Current UX Friction:** Browser password managers (1Password, LastPass, Bitwarden, Chrome Password Manager) frequently mistake administrative configuration inputs (such as the LDAP Bind Password or OAuth Client Secret) for the administrator personal sign-in credentials, triggering aggressive save/autofill prompts.
+- **Phase 2 Scope:**
+  - In `AuthCardEditorDrawer.tsx`, remove `type="password"` from `id="card-secret"` inputs (lines 964 and 1048).
+  - Add explicit password-manager suppression attributes to administrative credential inputs:
+    - `autoComplete="off"`
+    - `data-1p-ignore="true"`
+    - `data-lpignore="true"`
+    - `data-bwignore="true"`
+    - `data-form-type="other"`
+  - Render credential inputs strictly as `type="text"` with CSS masking (similar to `KAN-400`).
+
+### 3.7 Component Mount Isolation and RBAC View Routing
+- **Current UX Friction & Defect:**
+  - In `AuthStudioPage.tsx`, `<div id="panel-roles"><RbacPolicyBuilder isServerAdmin={true} /></div>` is mounted twice (lines 799-803 and lines 1019-1023).
+  - When `activeTab === roles`, the tab panels and ternary checks in lines 865-907 mount `panel-users` concurrently with `panel-roles`.
+  - The header action button renders `+ Add Local User` when `activeTab === roles` instead of hiding or rendering RBAC actions.
+- **Phase 2 Scope:**
+  - Remove duplicate `<div id="panel-roles">` mount block.
+  - Fix tab routing so each panel (`panel-cards`, `panel-users`, `panel-roles`) mounts strictly when its matching `activeTab` is active.
+  - Hide or contextually replace `+ Add Local User` button when `activeTab === roles`.
+  - Add bulk permission quick-selectors to `RbacPolicyBuilder.tsx` (e.g. "Select All Issue Permissions", "Clear Field Permissions").
+
